<title>USA: AMBAC says it qualifies seven muni bond issues.</title>
<headline>AMBAC says it qualifies seven muni bond issues.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMBAC Indemnity Corp said on Tuesday that it qualified for insurance the following seven municipal bond issues scheduled for competitive sale:</p>
<p>--Central Union High School, Calif., General Obligations (GOs), $5.15 million.</p>
<p>--Dawson County School District, Ga., GOs, $5.91 million.</p>
<p>--Quincy, Mass., GOs., $12.335 million.</p>
<p>--Shakopee, Minn., GOs, $3.14 million.</p>
<p>--St Louis County Housing Redevelopment, Minn., Revenue bonds, $5.275 million.</p>
<p>Bolivar-Richburg Central School District, N.Y., GOs, $2.865 million.</p>
<p>--Westbury, Unified School District, N.Y., $3 million.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
